ideas.first_experiment:
One day of work, no API cost. The lead runs each frozen leg once on 2022-2025.

Month-end leg, frozen as: last weekday of the month, 16:00:00 London, buy dollars if the S&P 500 is above its previous month-end close as of yesterday's close, otherwise sell; six pairs without the yen; exit 16:30; stop 1.5 x ATR24 on hourly bars; no filter on the size of the monthly move.

Pass, all required, measured on the 48 dates:
- basket net at least +1.5 bp per date;
- t on dates at least 2.0;
- at least 60 % of dates positive;
- at least 5 of 6 pairs positive;
- still positive with costs doubled.

If there is no effect this passes under 3 % of the time. If the full in-sample effect holds it passes about 88 % of the time; if half holds, about 35 %.

Tokyo leg, frozen as above. Pass: at least +1.0 bp net per settlement day for the pair of trades, t at least 2.0, positive in 3 of 4 years, and still above zero with entry and exit one minute late.

Before any money: record the real FP Markets spread at 16:00 London on two month-ends and at 09:55 Tokyo on ten settlement days.

